final_edits.new:
`super.init(…)` runs the C++ base constructor its arguments choose as `[FFI-57]` chooses a
  member of the base's `new` (the argument's own type before a coercion, argument by argument; none
  or a tie `E5035`) and runs it at `super.init(…)` (`[CLS-11]`);

`super.init(…)` selects the C++ base constructor as a call of the base's `new`
  selects a member (`[FFI-57]`: by its arguments' number, names, words and types, exact before
  coercion; none or a tie `E5035`) and runs it at `super.init(…)` (`[CLS-11]`);

* A `thread_shared` value is never placed in a frame; one made `using` a manager is counted away
  from its making line, the path chosen by its type (`[OPT-1]`, `[OBJ-4]`, `[ALC-1]`, `[RC-4]`,
  `[TYP-46a]`).
